<div class="pathway-content cr-page">
  <h1 class="page-header">&ldquo;After the Hurricane, Creating Art Was Healing&rdquo;</h1>

  <div class="video-embed align-right" style="margin-top: 20em; margin-bottom: 5em;">
    <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/3xVDCqSNoEE" title="YouTube video player" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
  </div>

  <div class="curator-msg float-right" style="width: 35em; max-width: 35em; margin-bottom: 3em; clear: right;">
    <p>Hurricane Irma destroyed Florida Keys-based artist Sally Binard&rsquo;s home in 2017. After the storm, she saw how &ldquo;everything that was on the inside of a person&rsquo;s home was on the outside&hellip;and everything that was in the inside of a person was was also on the outside.&rdquo; Her self-portrait &ldquo;Afraid to Launch,&rdquo; made out of found materials she salvaged from the wreckage of her home, evokes that sense of upheaval. The nails surrounding the artist&rsquo;s face show the inherent physicality as well as the artistic creativity required to rebuild after a storm.</p>

    <p>Learn more about <a class="link" href="/people/#sbinard">Sally Binard</a>.</p>
